# Note formatting in Cloud Foundry docs

Always use `<p class="note">` for notes. Never use markdown blockquote syntax (`>`).

Every note **must** include a `<span class="note__title">` as the **first element** on its own line immediately after the opening tag. This span provides the visible coloured label that distinguishes note severity levels.

The closing `</p>` must always be on its own line.

**Bad (markdown blockquote):**
```
> **Note** Some important information here.
```

**Bad (no note__title span, closing tag inline):**
```html
<p class="note">Some important information here.</p>
```

**Bad (missing note__title span):**
```html
<p class="note">Some important information here.
</p>
```

**Good:**
```html
<p class="note">
<span class="note__title"><strong>Note</strong></span>
Some important information here.
</p>
```

Use the appropriate class and title text for the severity level:

| Class | `<strong>` text | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `note` | `Note` | General informational notes |
| `note important` | `Important` | Important warnings the reader must not overlook |
| `note caution` | `Caution` | Actions that may cause data loss or irreversible changes |

```html
<p class="note important">
<span class="note__title"><strong>Important</strong></span>
This action cannot be undone.
</p>

<p class="note caution">
<span class="note__title"><strong>Caution</strong></span>
Deleting this service instance removes all associated data.
</p>
```

The same pattern applies to `<div class="note...">` wrappers — the `<span class="note__title">` is the first child element. Preserve the indentation level of the surrounding content when placing the span.
